  {
   "pagina": "https://elevenlabs.io/music/acoustic",
   "id": "81obftuook",
   "titulo": "Bright Horizons",
   "url": "https://eleven-public-cdn.elevenlabs.io/payloadcms/81obftuook.mp3",
   "etiquetas": [
    "The track is an upbeat and optimistic instrumental piece in the indie-folk or folk-pop genre. Its bright and catchy nature gives it a commercial or corporate-motivational feel, reminiscent of artists like The Lumineers but in a simplified, instrumental format.",
    "The arrangement is centered around a driving acoustic steel-string guitar. It's supported by a solid rhythm section consisting of a simple drum kit (kick, snare, hi-hats), a clean electric bass following the root notes, and percussion elements like a shaker and tambourine. A clean electric guitar adds melodic flourishes in the later sections.",
    "The song maintains a moderately fast tempo, approximately 125 BPM, in a standard 4/4 time signature. The rhythm is energetic and straightforward, driven by the consistent acoustic guitar strumming and a strong backbeat from the snare drum, creating a sense of forward momentum.",
    "The atmosphere is overwhelmingly positive, cheerful, and uplifting. It evokes feelings of optimism, hope, and celebration, making it feel inspiring and motivational.",
    "This is an instrumental track and contains no vocals.",
    "The song follows a conventional pop structure, building dynamically through layering. It begins with a solo acoustic guitar and gradually adds the bass, drums, and finally the melodic electric guitar, creating a clear progression from a sparse intro to a full, energetic chorus-like peak.",
    "A key feature is the use of a simple, repetitive, and highly memorable major-key chord progression. The arrangement's effectiveness comes from its gradual layering of instruments, which builds intensity and maintains listener engagement throughout the track."
   ]
  },
